# Origami Four Leaf Clover – Step-by-Step Diagram

## **Overview**

The four-leaf clover is one of the most recognizable symbols of luck. This traditional origami model is folded from a single square sheet of paper and uses repeated sink folds to create four symmetrical leaves.

This step-by-step diagram is suitable for folders with some previous origami experience, especially those familiar with sink folds. Once completed, the model can be used as a decoration, greeting card ornament, bookmark, or lucky gift.

### About this diagram

This diagram presents the complete folding sequence for a traditional **Origami Four-Leaf Clover**. The instructions were carefully illustrated to provide a clear, printable reference that is easier to follow than a video alone.

The finished model can be folded in different paper sizes and colors, making it suitable for decorations, greeting cards, scrapbooking, gifts, or St. Patrick's Day crafts.

